{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1203985-research-actions-for-ghost-spirits","id":1203985,"title":"research actions for ghost/spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-06T14:26:26-07:00","id":1203985,"title":"research actions for ghost/spirits","content":"The 2nd rule book makes mention of the need to use Int + Occult to do research on the target entity. How do you normally handle that in your games? Is the research mainly finding libraries and family history documents or do you use the research action as a type of on the scene investigation to find the anchor/resonant conditions in the haunted environment?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12209-adonus","name":"adonus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T15:44:34-07:00","id":1204016,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975865-2e-researching-supernaturals-in-game\"><b>Some fan take for 2E CoD rules on researching supernatural beings</b></a> - hunters are also take into account. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T17:06:15-07:00","id":1204037,"title":"","content":"You need context to do research. Just like you can't fix a car without tools, you can't research something without a body of documentation available. Look at examples of research in media: they don't give all the answers, but allow characters to have a better understanding of a situation if they don't mind eye-rolls at the inconceivable insanity they're spouting to more well adjusted people.<br /> <br /> Which usually means whichever phenomenon they're researched has happened before and was documented. The next thing is deducing connections between different events with arguably the same catalyst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}